+## Experimental VR Neural Rendering controls
+
+The Upscaling settings expose optional DLSS Neural Rendering experiments:
+
+- Eye-tracked crops have independent response, deadband, hold, prediction, quantization, and edge-margin controls. Gaze controls crop placement; adaptive quality controls crop size.
+- Sequential NR supports one to three evaluations on cropped regions. Two-pass NR can use a smaller, feathered second-pass region. With stage split enabled, only pass one can run before DLSS Super Resolution; later passes run after it.
+- Adaptive quality can reduce pass count, crop coverage, and NR processing resolution together. Its configurable order defaults to reducing passes first, then crop coverage, then NR resolution; restoration uses the reverse order.
+- Output controls adjust NR contribution, local detail, original scene colour and brightness, plus DLSS sharpening strength (0–5) and whether sharpening runs before or after NR.
+- Alternate-eye temporal residual reuse is experimental and restricted to VR single-pass NR. It reprojects the skipped eye using accumulated motion and resets both eye histories after large crop jumps; ghosting and cadence artifacts remain possible.
+
+Processing scales above 100% increase the NR input/output region resolution; they are not scene supersampling. New options use neutral defaults and remain opt-in. Validate them in-game on the target headset before relying on them for a regular playthrough.
+
 ## Build Instructions
 
